    "Changed map producer counts are initialized outside primary query loops, avoiding a new primary producer feedback. Partial-byte materialization alone is not the defect; producer liveness determines the edge.",
    "Split map full count MOVL is hoisted per round, spilled and reloaded per query. Paired MOVL remains adjacent to seeded BZHI, avoiding that count reload. AND map full mask is held invariant in a register.",
    "Map changed hit loops move into outlined ht::timed wrappers, whose entry/call is outside clocks. Actual measured CFGs have zero helper calls. This changes hoisting/field-load/register allocation and prevents instruction-parity claims.",
    "AND set arm9 exposes an untreated producer BZHI count edge: partial DL preserves previous primary selector mask RDX. Seeded split correctly uses AND; the remaining producer masking produces the new carried edge.",
    "Ordinary set arm9 uses fresh key-multiplier RAX before AL count; paired also uses fresh RAX for producer and full MOVL for split; split uses invariant producer and split counts. No analogous primary producer feedback in those inspected paths.",
    "Qualified primary first-candidate hit counts show no instruction/spill explosion: maps Zen ordinary56/split55/paired55/AND54; Granite55/54/54/53. Set arm9 Zen50/50/51/52; Granite49/49/51/51. Counts do not prove cycles or average lookup work."
